From: farjanatech <168655490+farjanatech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/RPi5: narrow SOCB producer resources for GPU sibling

The current SOCB ACPI0004 container advertises the complete BCM2712 legacy
MMIO aperture (0x107c000000-0x107fffffff) as a producer resource. GPU0 is a
sibling of SOCB, not its child, yet six of GPU0's display resources reside
inside that aperture. Windows reports the GPU device with Code 12 and
STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES.

Keep SOCB's DMA translation unchanged, but advertise only the MMIO ranges
actually consumed by its children in the Windows-oriented stack: PL011 and
the property-mailbox temperature provider added by the existing exp.5B
handoff patch. This removes GPU0 from the producer window without changing
any GPU, IRQ, DMA, fan, SD, Wi-Fi, PCIe, USB, framebuffer or boot settings.

This is an isolated hardware-test candidate; it does not claim that Code 12
is fixed until validated on the Raspberry Pi 5.
---
 Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/AcpiTables/Dsdt.asl | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/AcpiTables/Dsdt.asl b/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/AcpiTables/Dsdt.asl
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/AcpiTables/Dsdt.asl
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/RPi5/AcpiTables/Dsdt.asl
@@
       Method (_CRS, 0, Serialized) {
         //
-        // Container devices with _DMA must have _CRS.
-        // TO-DO: Is describing the entire MMIO range in a single resource
-        // enough, or do we need to list each individual resource consumed
-        // by the child devices?
+        // SOCB is a producer for its children only. Do not advertise the full
+        // BCM2712 legacy aperture here: GPU0 is a sibling and owns display
+        // resources inside that aperture.
         //
         Name (RBUF, ResourceTemplate () {
           QWORDMEMORY_BUF (00, ResourceProducer)
+          QWORDMEMORY_BUF (01, ResourceProducer)
         })
-        QWORD_SET (00, BCM2712_LEGACY_BUS_BASE, BCM2712_LEGACY_BUS_LENGTH, 0)
+        QWORD_SET (00, PL011_DEBUG_BASE_ADDRESS, PL011_DEBUG_LENGTH, 0)
+        // TMP0 is added by the existing Windows fan-safe handoff patch.
+        QWORD_SET (01, 0x000000107C013880, 0x40, 0)
         Return (RBUF)
       }
